          "claim": "For $\\mathbf n\\in S^2$, $P_T(\\mathbf n)=I-\\mathbf n\\mathbf n^\\top$ is an orthogonal projection and [A2] gives $\\mathbf n\\cdot b(\\mathbf n)=0$; hence $\\mathbf k\\cdot f_\\epsilon(\\mathbf k)=0$ a.e. Since $\\epsilon<|\\mathbf k|<\\kappa$ on the support, the radial norm integrals in [F4]–[F6] are finite on these strictly positive finite bounds, so both $f_\\epsilon$ and $\\omega f_\\epsilon$ are square-integrable.",
