          "id": "lem-qft-qed-coherent-ir-obstruction-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For any $u,v\\in\\mathcal H_T$, [F2] gives $\\langle u^{\\otimes n},v^{\\otimes n}\\rangle=\\langle u,v\\rangle^n$ and $\\|u^{\\otimes n}\\|^2=\\|u\\|^{2n}$. By [F7]–[F8], $\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\|u\\|^{2n}/n!=e^{\\|u\\|^2}<\\infty$, so the displayed $\\epsilon(u)$ belongs to symmetric Fock space. Its direct-sum pairing with $\\epsilon(v)$ is the absolutely convergent series $\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\langle u,v\\rangle^n/n!=e^{\\langle u,v\\rangle}$, by [F7]. The addition and modulus laws [F8]–[F9] therefore give that $C(u)$ has norm one and $|\\langle C(u),C(v)\\rangle|=e^{-\\|u-v\\|^2/2}$. This direct tensor calculation requires no separability hypothesis on $\\mathcal H_T$. On the full vector space $L^2(\\mathbb R^3;\\mathbb C^3)$, multiplication by $\\omega$ commutes with the multiplier $P_T$. Its tensor-power projections therefore commute with the sector multiplier $\\sum_j|\\mathbf k_j|$; the transverse symmetric Fock space is a reducing subspace for the second-quantized multiplier of [F3]. If $r=\\|f_\\epsilon\\|^2$, $q=\\langle f_\\epsilon,\\omega f_\\epsilon\\rangle$, and $s=\\|\\omega f_\\epsilon\\|^2$, the sector formulas give\n$$ \\|d\\Gamma(\\omega)C(f_\\epsilon)\\|^2 =e^{-r}\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\frac{n s r^{n-1}+n(n-1)q^2r^{n-2}}{n!} =s+q^2<\\infty. $$\nThe same sector sum with one multiplier gives $\\langle C(f_\\epsilon),d\\Gamma(\\omega)C(f_\\epsilon)\\rangle=q$; [F2] gives $\\|C(f_\\epsilon)\\|=1$. Multiplying by $\\hbar c$ and substituting [step 1.2] proves the stated domain and energy claims.",
          "step": "2.1",
