      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "def-countable-choice",
          "carrier": "items/def-countable-choice.md",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "The **Axiom of Countable Choice**, written $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$, is the following\nstatement.",
          "consumer_use": "A1 in step 1.1, step 1.2, step 3.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "def-qft-qed-photon-energy-multiplier",
          "carrier": "items/def-qft-qed-photon-energy-multiplier.md",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Use the transverse space $\\mathcal H_T=\\operatorname{Ran}M_{P_T}$ of [[def-qft-photon-transverse-space]], with $P_T(\\mathbf k)=I_3-\\mathbf n\\mathbf n^T$ for $\\mathbf k\\ne0$ and any assigned value at the null point $\\mathbf k=0$. In the QFT length convention, assign $\\mathbf k$ units m$^{-1}$ and define the nonnegative measurable multiplier\n$$\n\\omega(\\mathbf k):=|\\mathbf k|.\n$$\nIts maximal multiplication operator on $\\mathcal H_T$ is\n$$\n(M_\\omega f)(\\mathbf k):=\\omega(\\mathbf k)f(\\mathbf k),\\qquad\nD(M_\\omega):=\\{f\\in\\mathcal H_T:\\omega f\\in L^2(\\mathbb R^3,d^3\\mathbf k;\\mathbb C^3)\\}.\n$$\nBecause $\\omega$ is a scalar multiplier, $\\mathbf k\\cdot f(\\mathbf k)=0$ a.e. implies $\\mathbf k\\cdot(M_\\omega f)(\\mathbf k)=0$ a.e.; thus the displayed multiplication maps its stated domain into $\\mathcal H_T$. The value $\\omega(0)=0$ is immaterial to the $L^2$ operator. For $\\hbar,c>0$, the corresponding one-particle energy convention is $E_1:=\\hbar c M_\\omega$, in joules.",
          "consumer_use": "F1 in step 1.1, step 1.2",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum",
          "carrier": "items/lem-qft-second-quantized-spectrum.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]]. Let\n$(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be a sigma-finite measure space and let\n$\\boldsymbol\\omega=(\\omega_1,\\ldots,\\omega_d):X\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be a\nfinite-valued measurable map, where $d\\ge1$. Put\n$H=L^2(X,\\mu;\\mathbb C)$ with the second-variable-linear pairing of\n[[def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces]], and form the bosonic Fock space\n$\\mathcal F_s(H)$. For $n\\ge1$, identify $H_s^{(n)}$ with the symmetric\nsubspace of $L^2(X^n,\\overline{\\mu^{\\times n}};\\mathbb C)$ by iterating\n[[lem-qft-l2-product-tensor-identification]]. Set $X^0=\\{\\star\\}$,\n$s_0(\\star)=0$, and for $n\\ge1$ set\n$$s_n(x_1,\\ldots,x_n)=\\sum_{r=1}^n\\boldsymbol\\omega(x_r)\\in\\mathbb R^d.$$\nFor $1\\le j\\le d$, define $H_j$ by multiplication by the $j$th coordinate\n$s_{n,j}$ on sector $n$, with exact domain\n$$D(H_j)=\\left\\{\\Psi=(\\Psi_n): \\sum_{n\\ge1}\\int_{X^n}|s_{n,j}|^2|\\Psi_n|^2\\,d\\overline{\\mu^{\\times n}}<\\infty\\right\\}.$$\nEach $H_j$ is self-adjoint, and $\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}\\cap D(H_j)$ is a\ngraph core. The joint projection-valued measure\n[[def-projection-valued-measure]] on $\\mathbb R^d$ is\n$$(E(B)\\Psi)_n=\\mathbf1_{s_n^{-1}(B)}\\Psi_n\\quad(n\\ge1),\\qquad (E(B)\\Psi)_0=\\mathbf1_B(0)\\Psi_0.$$\nFor $\\theta\\in\\mathbb R^d$, let $H_\\theta$ be multiplication on sector $n$\nby $\\theta\\cdot s_n$, with its maximal square-integrability domain. Then\n$$U_\\theta(t)\\Psi:=\\bigl(e^{it\\theta\\cdot s_n}\\Psi_n\\bigr)_{n\\ge0}$$\nis a strongly continuous unitary group on all of Fock space, and its norm\nderivative at zero exists exactly for $\\Psi\\in D(H_\\theta)$, where it is\n$iH_\\theta\\Psi$. The zero-particle sector is the vacuum eigenvector at joint\nvalue $0$.",
          "consumer_use": "F3 in step 2.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
          "carrier": "items/def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces.md",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "For an integer $d\\ge1$, let $\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R^d)$ be the complex Schwartz space with seminorms\n$p_{\\alpha\\beta}(f)=\\sup_{x\\in\\mathbb R^d}|x^\\alpha\\partial^\\beta f(x)|$\nfor all multi-indices $\\alpha,\\beta$; this is exactly\n[[def-schwartz-space-and-its-seminorms]]. Let\n$\\mathcal D(\\mathbb R^d)=C_c^\\infty(\\mathbb R^d;\\mathbb C)$ with the support convention of\n[[def-test-function-space-d-of-an-open-set]] and the locally convex LF topology of\n[[def-test-function-topology]]. The tempered-distribution space $\\mathcal S'(\\mathbb R^d)$\nis the space of continuous complex-linear functionals on this topological\n$\\mathcal S(\\mathbb R^d)$, paired bilinearly with test functions, as in\n[[def-tempered-distribution]].\n\nFor every complex Hilbert space $H$, use the second-variable-linear pairing\n$\\langle u,v\\rangle_2:=(v,u)_1$, where $(\\cdot,\\cdot)_1$ is the first-variable-linear\nHilbert pairing of [[def-real-and-complex-inner-product-space]]. Thus\n$\\langle u,v\\rangle_2$ is linear in $v$ and conjugate-linear in $u$.\nFor each tensor product, use the same norm completion as\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-hilbert-tensor-construction]], but equip it with the\nsecond-variable-linear pairing obtained by conjugating that supplier's\nfirst-variable-linear pairing. This leaves the norm and completion unchanged;\non elementary tensors it gives the product of the second-variable pairings.\nLet $H^{\\widehat\\otimes n}$ be the iterated Hilbert tensor completion, with\n$H^{\\widehat\\otimes0}:=\\mathbb C$; the tensor inner product is the product of\nthe factor pairings. For $n\\ge1$, let\n$P_{s,n}=n!^{-1}\\sum_{\\pi\\in S_n}U_\\pi$ and\n$P_{a,n}=n!^{-1}\\sum_{\\pi\\in S_n}\\operatorname{sgn}(\\pi)U_\\pi$, using the\npermutation action and the orthogonal projections of\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-permutation-sector-projections]]. Define\n$H_s^{(n)}=\\operatorname{ran}P_{s,n}$ and\n$H_a^{(n)}=\\operatorname{ran}P_{a,n}$, with\n$H_s^{(0)}=H_a^{(0)}=\\mathbb C$. These are the symmetric and antisymmetric\n$n$-particle sectors.\n\nThe bosonic and fermionic Fock Hilbert spaces are the square-summable direct\nsums\n$\\mathcal F_s(H)=\\{(\\Psi_n)_{n\\ge0}:\\Psi_n\\in H_s^{(n)},\\\n\\sum_n\\|\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\}$ and\n$\\mathcal F_a(H)=\\{(\\Psi_n)_{n\\ge0}:\\Psi_n\\in H_a^{(n)},\\\n\\sum_n\\|\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\}$, with the componentwise inner product.\nTheir vacuum is $\\Omega=(1,0,0,\\ldots)$. The finite-particle subspace\n$\\mathcal D_{\\rm fin}$ consists of sequences with only finitely many nonzero\ncomponents.\n\nFor $n\\ge0$, bosonic creation on sector $n$ is\n$a_n^\\dagger(h)\\Psi_n=\\sqrt{n+1}P_{s,n+1}(h\\otimes\\Psi_n)$; for $n\\ge1$,\nbosonic annihilation is\n$a_n(h)\\Psi_n=\\sqrt n(C_h\\otimes I^{\\otimes(n-1)})\\Psi_n$, where\n$C_h(v)=\\langle h,v\\rangle_2$ and its tensor extension is the bounded map of\n[[lem-nrqm-composites-bounded-tensor-maps]], and $a(h)\\Omega=0$. Define fermionic creation\nby $c_n^\\dagger(h)\\Psi_n=\\sqrt{n+1}P_{a,n+1}(h\\otimes\\Psi_n)$; for $n\\ge1$,\nfermionic annihilation is the corresponding first-factor contraction\n$c_n(h)\\Psi_n=\\sqrt n(C_h\\otimes I^{\\otimes(n-1)})\\Psi_n$, and\n$c(h)\\Omega=0$. The annihilation maps are conjugate-linear in $h$; the\ncreation maps are linear in $h$. These formulas define sector maps on the\nfinite-particle subspace; their maximal closed domains and operator relations are proved in\n[[lem-qft-fock-ccr-car]]. No physical statistics assignment or spin–statistics\ntheorem is part of these mathematical definitions.",
          "consumer_use": "F2 in step 2.1, step 3.1, step 4.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface",
          "carrier": "items/def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface.md",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Assume the $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ convention of [[def-bounded-c-one-domain-boundary-charts-and-outward-normal]]. Let S be a compact embedded $C^1$ hypersurface in $\\mathbb R^n$, $n\\ge2$. Choose finitely many regular injective $C^1$ parametrizations $X_j:V_j\\to S\\cap O_j$ with $C^1$ coordinate transitions, and an ambient partition $\\chi_j$ from [[lem-finite-ambient-partitions-for-euclidean-boundary-integration]], with supports compactly contained in the corresponding chart neighborhoods. Put $J_{X_j}=\\sqrt{\\det(DX_j^TDX_j)}$, using [[def-gram-matrix-and-gram-determinant]].\n\nFor a nonnegative Borel f on S define $\\int_S f\\,dS=\\sum_j\\int_{V_j}(\\chi_j f)(X_j(y))J_{X_j}(y)\\,dy$, where the integrals on the right are those of [[def-nonnegative-lebesgue-integral]] and $0\\cdot\\infty=0$. Set $S(A)=\\int_S\\mathbf1_A\\,dS$ for Borel A. For signed f with $\\int_S|f|\\,dS<\\infty$ use the difference of the positive and negative integrals. The same chart formula restricts to a compact Borel face contained in a regular patch. The empty surface has zero integral. Independence and finiteness are established by the following chart-independence lemma.",
          "consumer_use": "F4 in step 1.1, step 1.2, step 3.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "lem-euclidean-chart-measure-agrees-with-polar-surface-measure",
          "carrier": "items/lem-euclidean-chart-measure-agrees-with-polar-surface-measure.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ and $n\\ge2$. The chart surface measure on $S^{n-1}$ equals the polar measure $\\sigma$. Orthogonal transformations preserve it. The map $\\omega\\mapsto a+R\\omega$, $R>0$, multiplies surface measure by $R^{n-1}$, and $|S^{n-1}|=n|B_1|$.",
          "consumer_use": "F5 in step 1.1, step 1.2, step 3.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
