          "supplier": "def-complex-exponential",
          "carrier": "items/def-complex-exponential.md",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Let $\\iota_{\\mathbb R}\\colon\\mathbb N\\to\\mathbb R$ be the canonical-natural map\nof [[def-canonical-natural]], and let $j\\colon\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb C$ be the real\nembedding $j(x)=x+i0$ from [[def-complex-numbers-and-arithmetic]]. For every\n$n\\in\\mathbb N$, the factorial $n!$ is nonzero by\n[[def-factorial-and-falling-factorial]], so\n$\\iota_{\\mathbb R}(n!)>0$ by [[lem-of-naturals-positive]] and consequently\n$j(\\iota_{\\mathbb R}(n!))\\ne0$ in the complex field\n[[thm-complex-numbers-form-a-field]].\n\nFor $z\\in\\mathbb C$, define\n$$ \\exp z:=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\\frac{z^n}{j(\\iota_{\\mathbb R}(n!))}. $$\nwhenever this complex series converges. Inside a complex expression we\nabbreviate the embedded denominator $j(\\iota_{\\mathbb R}(n!))$ by $n!$, so the\nsame definition may be written $\\exp z=\\sum z^n/n!$ without identifying a\nnatural number with a complex number. Powers and series are those of\n[[def-complex-integer-powers]] and\n[[def-complex-series-power-series-and-absolute-convergence]]. The convergence\nfor every $z\\in\\mathbb C$ is discharged by\n[[lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere]].",
          "consumer_use": "F7 in step 2.1, step 4.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere",
          "carrier": "items/lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "For every $z\\in\\mathbb C$, the series $\\sum z^n/n!$ converges absolutely.",
          "consumer_use": "F7 in step 2.1, step 4.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "thm-complex-exponential-addition-and-real-extension",
          "carrier": "items/thm-complex-exponential-addition-and-real-extension.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "For all $z,w\\in\\mathbb C$, $\\exp(z+w)=\\exp z\\exp w$. For real $x$, the complex value $\\exp(x+0i)$ equals the published real exponential $e^x$. The conventions and prerequisite facts used below are recorded in [[def-complex-exponential]], [[lem-complex-exponential-series-converges-everywhere]], [[lem-cauchy-product-of-absolutely-convergent-complex-series]], [[def-real-exponential-function-and-e]], [[lem-binomial-theorem-over-complex-numbers]], [[thm-binomial-closed-formula]].",
          "consumer_use": "F8 in step 2.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        },
        {
          "supplier": "cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity",
          "carrier": "items/cor-complex-exponential-cartesian-form-modulus-and-eulers-identity.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "For real $x,y$, $\\exp(x+iy)=e^x(\\cos y+i\\sin y)$ and $|\\exp(x+iy)|=e^x$. In particular $e^{i\\pi}+1=0$. The conventions and prerequisite facts used below are recorded in [[thm-complex-exponential-addition-and-real-extension]], [[thm-eulers-formula]], [[lem-complex-conjugation-and-modulus-laws]], [[thm-pythagorean-and-parity-identities-for-all-six-trigonometric-functions]], [[cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity]], [[thm-quarter-turn-values-and-shift-formulas]], [[def-pi-via-first-positive-cosine-zero]].",
          "consumer_use": "F9 in step 2.1",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Actual carrier interface inspected; native workflow acceptance remains separate."
        }
      ],
