    "lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "lem-qft-qed-tree-ward",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Use the $(-+++)$ coordinate convention, $h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, and the Clifford matrices of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]; the shell parameter $\\mu>0$ has inverse-length units as in [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. For $p=(p^0,\\mathbf p)\\in\\mathbb R^4$, write\n$$\n\\Gamma(p):=\\gamma^0p^0-\\sum_{j=1}^3\\gamma^jp_j,\\qquad\nK(p):=\\Gamma(p)-\\mu I_4.\n$$\nWhen $h(p,p)\\ne\\mu^2$, define the finite rational inverse\n$$\nS_0(p):=\\frac{\\Gamma(p)+\\mu I_4}{h(p,p)-\\mu^2}.\n$$\nFor $p,p+k$ with both denominators nonzero,\n$$\nS_0(p+k)\\Gamma(k)S_0(p)=S_0(p)-S_0(p+k).\n$$\nFor any finite chain of off-shell momenta, the corresponding insertion differences telescope with both endpoint terms retained. If $u(p),u(p')$ satisfy $(\\Gamma(p)-\\mu)u(p)=0$, $(\\Gamma(p')-\\mu)u(p')=0$ and $p,p'$ lie on the future shell, then $\\bar u(p')\\Gamma(p-p')u(p)=0$, where $\\bar u=u^\\dagger\\beta$. If $v(q)$ satisfies $(\\Gamma(q)+\\mu)v(q)=0$ on the future shell, then $\\bar v(q)\\Gamma(p+q)u(p)=0$. These are finite rational/tree identities; no Feynman boundary value, singular distribution product, loop theorem, or all-diagram gauge-independence claim is included.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge-step-1-1",
          "claim": "The first line has transfer $p_1-p_1'=k$, so [F1] gives $k_\\mu J_1^\\mu=0$. The second line has transfer $p_2-p_2'=-k$, so $(-k)_\\nu J_2^\\nu=0$, hence $k_\\nu J_2^\\nu=0$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge-step-1-2",
          "claim": "Contracting the longitudinal kernel gives\n$\nJ_1^\\mu\\Delta D_{\\mu\\nu}(k)J_2^\\nu\n=c(k)(k_\\mu J_1^\\mu)(k_\\nu J_2^\\nu)=0\n$ \nby [step 1.1].",
          "step": "1.2",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge-step-2-1",
          "claim": "For a tree current with $k_\\mu J^\\mu=0$, the change under $\\epsilon^\\mu\\mapsto\\epsilon^\\mu+\\alpha k^\\mu$ is $\\alpha k_\\mu J^\\mu=0$. This proves the polarization claim for the explicit current types of [F1].",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "A1",
            "F1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "routine_steps": [],
      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "If either current is zero, the contraction vanishes directly in step 1.2."
        },
        {
          "case": "zero",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "At k=0, step 1.2 has c(0)k_mu k_nu=0; A1 makes c(0) finite."
        },
        {
          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "The lem-qft-qed-conserved-current-gauge claim makes no one boundary assertion."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "not_applicable",
