      ],
      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "lem-qft-qed-tree-ward",
          "carrier": "items/lem-qft-qed-tree-ward.md",
          "status": "current batch-45 draft supplier; full proof inspected",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Use the $(-+++)$ coordinate convention, $h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, and the Clifford matrices of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]; the shell parameter $\\mu>0$ has inverse-length units as in [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. For $p=(p^0,\\mathbf p)\\in\\mathbb R^4$, write\n$$\n\\Gamma(p):=\\gamma^0p^0-\\sum_{j=1}^3\\gamma^jp_j,\\qquad\nK(p):=\\Gamma(p)-\\mu I_4.\n$$\nWhen $h(p,p)\\ne\\mu^2$, define the finite rational inverse\n$$\nS_0(p):=\\frac{\\Gamma(p)+\\mu I_4}{h(p,p)-\\mu^2}.\n$$\nFor $p,p+k$ with both denominators nonzero,\n$$\nS_0(p+k)\\Gamma(k)S_0(p)=S_0(p)-S_0(p+k).\n$$\nFor any finite chain of off-shell momenta, the corresponding insertion differences telescope with both endpoint terms retained. If $u(p),u(p')$ satisfy $(\\Gamma(p)-\\mu)u(p)=0$, $(\\Gamma(p')-\\mu)u(p')=0$ and $p,p'$ lie on the future shell, then $\\bar u(p')\\Gamma(p-p')u(p)=0$, where $\\bar u=u^\\dagger\\beta$. If $v(q)$ satisfies $(\\Gamma(q)+\\mu)v(q)=0$ on the future shell, then $\\bar v(q)\\Gamma(p+q)u(p)=0$. These are finite rational/tree identities; no Feynman boundary value, singular distribution product, loop theorem, or all-diagram gauge-independence claim is included.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F1] [[lem-qft-qed-tree-ward]]: for each stated on-shell Dirac current, contraction with its momentum transfer is zero; the proof uses the fixed $h=-\\eta$ slash convention.\nConsumer uses: 1.1, 2.1.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current assigned draft; proof is complete here, but readiness is escalated through upstream draft inputs.",
          "consumer_use": "F1 is used in step 1.1; step 2.1"
