      ],
      "supplier_excerpts": [
        {
          "supplier": "lem-qft-qed-tree-ward",
          "carrier": "items/lem-qft-qed-tree-ward.md",
          "status": "current batch-45 draft supplier; full proof inspected",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Use the $(-+++)$ coordinate convention, $h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, and the Clifford matrices of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]; the shell parameter $\\mu>0$ has inverse-length units as in [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. For $p=(p^0,\\mathbf p)\\in\\mathbb R^4$, write\n$$\n\\Gamma(p):=\\gamma^0p^0-\\sum_{j=1}^3\\gamma^jp_j,\\qquad\nK(p):=\\Gamma(p)-\\mu I_4.\n$$\nWhen $h(p,p)\\ne\\mu^2$, define the finite rational inverse\n$$\nS_0(p):=\\frac{\\Gamma(p)+\\mu I_4}{h(p,p)-\\mu^2}.\n$$\nFor $p,p+k$ with both denominators nonzero,\n$$\nS_0(p+k)\\Gamma(k)S_0(p)=S_0(p)-S_0(p+k).\n$$\nFor any finite chain of off-shell momenta, the corresponding insertion differences telescope with both endpoint terms retained. If $u(p),u(p')$ satisfy $(\\Gamma(p)-\\mu)u(p)=0$, $(\\Gamma(p')-\\mu)u(p')=0$ and $p,p'$ lie on the future shell, then $\\bar u(p')\\Gamma(p-p')u(p)=0$, where $\\bar u=u^\\dagger\\beta$. If $v(q)$ satisfies $(\\Gamma(q)+\\mu)v(q)=0$ on the future shell, then $\\bar v(q)\\Gamma(p+q)u(p)=0$. These are finite rational/tree identities; no Feynman boundary value, singular distribution product, loop theorem, or all-diagram gauge-independence claim is included.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F1] [[lem-qft-qed-tree-ward]]: when both $h(p,p)-\\mu^2$ and $h(p+k,p+k)-\\mu^2$ are nonzero, $S_0(p)=(\\Gamma(p)+\\mu I_4)/(h(p,p)-\\mu^2)$ and $S_0(p+k)\\Gamma(k)S_0(p)=S_0(p)-S_0(p+k)$.\nConsumer uses: 1.1, 1.2.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current assigned draft; proof is complete here, but readiness is escalated through upstream draft inputs.",
          "consumer_use": "F1 is used in step 1.1; step 1.2"
        },
        {
          "supplier": "def-qft-dirac-projections",
          "carrier": "items/def-qft-dirac-projections.md",
          "status": "current QFT-MF03 draft supplier; statement and proof inspected",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "exact_statement": "Use the Pauli matrices $\\sigma_1=\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$, $\\sigma_2=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\\\i&0\\end{pmatrix}$, and $\\sigma_3=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$. On $\\mathbb C^4=\\mathbb C^2\\oplus\\mathbb C^2$, define\n$$\\beta=\\begin{pmatrix}I_2&0\\\\0&-I_2\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\alpha_j=\\begin{pmatrix}0&\\sigma_j\\\\\\sigma_j&0\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\gamma^0=\\beta,\\qquad \\gamma^j=\\beta\\alpha_j.$$\nFor a spinor column $z\\in\\mathbb C^4$, its Dirac adjoint is $\\bar z=z^\\dagger\\beta$. The Clifford contraction is $\\Gamma(p):=\\gamma^0p^0-\\sum_{j=1}^3\\gamma^jp_j$; this contraction uses the effective matrix $-\\eta$ in the relation $\\{\\gamma^a,\\gamma^b\\}=-2\\eta^{ab}I_4$.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[F2] [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]: $\\beta=\\operatorname{diag}(I_2,-I_2)$, so $\\beta^2=I_4$; the item fixes $\\Gamma(p)$ with the effective matrix $h=-\\eta$.\nConsumer uses: 1.2.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Draft definition and conditional argument inspected; its Step 1 record is escalated because upstream page edges remain open.",
          "consumer_use": "F2 is used in step 1.2"
        },
        {
          "supplier": "lem-qft-qed-tree-ward",
          "carrier": "items/lem-qft-qed-tree-ward.md",
          "status": "current batch-45 draft supplier; full proof inspected",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Use the $(-+++)$ coordinate convention, $h=-\\eta=\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,-1,-1)$, and the Clifford matrices of [[def-qft-dirac-projections]]; the shell parameter $\\mu>0$ has inverse-length units as in [[def-qft-scalar-mass-shell]]. For $p=(p^0,\\mathbf p)\\in\\mathbb R^4$, write\n$$\n\\Gamma(p):=\\gamma^0p^0-\\sum_{j=1}^3\\gamma^jp_j,\\qquad\nK(p):=\\Gamma(p)-\\mu I_4.\n$$\nWhen $h(p,p)\\ne\\mu^2$, define the finite rational inverse\n$$\nS_0(p):=\\frac{\\Gamma(p)+\\mu I_4}{h(p,p)-\\mu^2}.\n$$\nFor $p,p+k$ with both denominators nonzero,\n$$\nS_0(p+k)\\Gamma(k)S_0(p)=S_0(p)-S_0(p+k).\n$$\nFor any finite chain of off-shell momenta, the corresponding insertion differences telescope with both endpoint terms retained. If $u(p),u(p')$ satisfy $(\\Gamma(p)-\\mu)u(p)=0$, $(\\Gamma(p')-\\mu)u(p')=0$ and $p,p'$ lie on the future shell, then $\\bar u(p')\\Gamma(p-p')u(p)=0$, where $\\bar u=u^\\dagger\\beta$. If $v(q)$ satisfies $(\\Gamma(q)+\\mu)v(q)=0$ on the future shell, then $\\bar v(q)\\Gamma(p+q)u(p)=0$. These are finite rational/tree identities; no Feynman boundary value, singular distribution product, loop theorem, or all-diagram gauge-independence claim is included.",
          "relevant_hypotheses_and_conventions": "[A1] $\\mu>0$ has inverse-length units; the momenta $p=0$ and $k=(2\\mu,0,0,0)$ use the same inverse-length coordinate convention as [[lem-qft-qed-tree-ward]].\nConsumer uses: 1.1.",
          "supplier_proof_status": "Current assigned draft; proof is complete here, but readiness is escalated through upstream draft inputs.",
          "consumer_use": "A1 is used in step 1.1"
        }
      ],
      "risk_review": {
